$$
\#\text{covered}\le C\sqrt P\sum_\tau\sqrt{W_\tau}+CX
\le C\sqrt P\,X^{3/2}+CX.
$$

Covering $\asymp P$ candidates forces $X\gg P^{1/3}=N^{1/6}$. Higher-degree support-$k$, degree-$e$ targets have the source bound $CP^{1-e/k}W^{1/k}+C$; Hölder and $k\le2e$, $e\ge2$, give the $N^{1/5}$ branch. T1’s different, true-pair count is proved in §8 rather than replacing actual primes by all candidates.

